{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011fWVBVgdQ53LEfTxg5aQQT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Standard Operating Procedures\n     2→\n     3→This document captures the development conventions, release workflow, and operational norms for the Hankweave codebase. Written for humans and AI agents working in the repo.\n     4→\n     5→Last updated: 2026-02-14 (v0.4.1).\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## 1. Repository Structure\n    10→\n    11→```\n    12→hankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n    13→├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n    14→├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n    15→├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n    16→├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n    17→├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n    18→├── docs/                   ← documentation site workspace (Next.js + Nextra)\n    19→│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n    20→│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n    21→│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n    22→│   ├── public/             ← static assets + generated schemas\n    23→│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n    24→├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n    25→├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n    26→├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n    27→├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n    28→├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n    29→├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n    30→├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n    31→├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n    32→└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm) + workspace root\n    33→```\n    34→\n    35→The documentation site (`docs/`) deploys to Vercel from this repo. It is a Bun workspace but does not have a workspace dependency on the runtime package.\n    36→\n    37→There is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n    38→\n    39→### What gets stripped before public release\n    40→\n    41→The sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n    42→\n    43→- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`, `docs/`\n    44→- **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n    45→\n    46→The `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n    47→\n    48→The `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, `release:*` scripts are removed, and the `workspaces` field is deleted (since docs are not included in the public repo).\n    49→\n    50→---\n    51→\n    52→## 2. Branch Model\n    53→\n    54→```\n    55→feature branches → develop → release/alpha\n    56→                      ↑\n    57→              all PRs target here\n    58→```\n    59→\n    60→- **`develop`** — active development. All PRs target this branch. All work starts here.\n    61→- **`release/alpha`** — the default branch on GitHub. Customer-facing. Tagged releases are cut from here. Never commit directly to release/alpha; it receives merges from develop only during the release process.\n    62→- **No `main` or `master` branch.** This is intentional.\n    63→\n    64→### Feature branch naming\n    65→\n    66→- Author-prefixed: `hrishi/sentinel-qol-fixes`, `hrishi/init-wizard`\n    67→- Descriptive: `fix/loop-iteration-telemetry`, `shim-timeout`\n    68→- Ticket-based: `ENG-90`\n    69→\n    70→The `hrishi/*` prefix is Hrishi's convention for easier identification. Philip uses bare names. Either is fine.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43c754e8-4bc1-4bd6-9886-b45962e4c4e6","uuid":"eb13af73-db01-4541-875f-d107fbe886ae","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md","content":"# Standard Operating Procedures\n\nThis document captures the development conventions, release workflow, and operational norms for the Hankweave codebase. Written for humans and AI agents working in the repo.\n\nLast updated: 2026-02-14 (v0.4.1).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Repository Structure\n\n```\nhankweave-dev/              ← private repo (SouthBridgeAI/hankweave)\n├── server/                 ← runtime source code (TypeScript, Bun)\n├── scripts/                ← build, release, sync, and dev tooling\n├── tests/                  ← unit, integration, e2e, cross-runtime\n├── schemas/                ← generated JSON schemas (from Zod)\n├── shims/                  ← agent harness adapters\n├── docs/                   ← documentation site workspace (Next.js + Nextra)\n│   ├── app/                ← Next.js app directory\n│   ├── content/            ← MDX documentation pages\n│   ├── components/         ← custom React components\n│   ├── public/             ← static assets + generated schemas\n│   └── package.json        ← hankweave-docs workspace\n├── learning/               ← example hanks and guides (ships to public)\n├── intermediates/          ← planning docs, numbered by feature (internal only)\n├── external-docs/          ← SDK reference docs for agent context (internal only)\n├── public-release-files/   ← files overlaid onto the public repo during sync\n├── assets/                 ← images, demo GIFs\n├── .github/                ← CI workflows and composite actions\n├── CHANGELOG.md            ← Keep a Changelog format, [Unreleased] workflow\n├── CONTRIBUTING.md         ← branch model and PR guidelines (internal only)\n└── package.json            ← @southbridgeai/hankweave (private npm) + workspace root\n```\n\nThe documentation site (`docs/`) deploys to Vercel from this repo. It is a Bun workspace but does not have a workspace dependency on the runtime package.\n\nThere is a separate public repo at `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime` which receives sanitized snapshots via the sync workflow. It publishes the public `hankweave` npm package.\n\n### What gets stripped before public release\n\nThe sync process (`scripts/sync-public.ts`) removes internal-only content:\n\n- **Directories**: `intermediates/`, `external-docs/`, `public-release-files/`, `.github/actions/`, `docs/`\n- **Files**: `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `PUBLISHING-PLAN.md`, `telemetry.md` (root), `reference/telemetry.md` (internal version), `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/sync-public.yml`, `scripts/sync-public.ts`, `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`, `scripts/release.ts`, `.DS_Store`\n\nThe `public-release-files/` directory contains replacements that get overlaid: a public-facing `README.md`, `LICENSE.md`, `NOTICE.md`, a sanitized `reference/telemetry.md`, and a simplified `.github/workflows/release.yml`.\n\nThe `package.json` is transformed: name becomes `hankweave`, `publishConfig.access` becomes `public`, `homepage` points to the public repo, `release:*` scripts are removed, and the `workspaces` field is deleted (since docs are not included in the public repo).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Branch Model\n\n```\nfeature branches → develop → release/alpha\n                      ↑\n              all PRs target here\n```\n\n- **`develop`** — active development. All PRs target this branch. All work starts here.\n- **`release/alpha`** — the default branch on GitHub. Customer-facing. Tagged releases are cut from here. Never commit directly to release/alpha; it receives merges from develop only during the release process.\n- **No `main` or `master` branch.** This is intentional.\n\n### Feature branch naming\n\n- Author-prefixed: `hrishi/sentinel-qol-fixes`, `hrishi/init-wizard`\n- Descriptive: `fix/loop-iteration-telemetry`, `shim-timeout`\n- Ticket-based: `ENG-90`\n\nThe `hrishi/*` prefix is Hrishi's convention for easier identification. Philip uses bare names. Either is fine.","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":429}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:01:47.586Z"}
