{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CfZ3onv1xBkQkcZq3Swxaa","type":"tool_result","content":"   303→**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n   304→\n   305→```bash\n   306→cd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n   307→```\n   308→\n   309→Verify the Next.js build succeeds. The `postbuild` step (Pagefind search indexing) should also run. If the build fails, the most likely cause is module resolution issues due to dependency hoisting. Bun workspaces hoist dependencies to the root `node_modules/`. The docs' dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, etc.) will land in the root `node_modules/`, not `docs/node_modules/`. ESM imports from `docs/next.config.mjs` (e.g., `import nextra from 'nextra'`) should resolve via Node's upward traversal, but if they don't, the fallback is to run `bun install` explicitly from `docs/` to create a local `node_modules/` with symlinks.\n   310→\n   311→### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n   312→\n   313→**Step 2.1: Exclude `docs/` from root `tsconfig.json`**\n   314→\n   315→The root `tsconfig.json` has `\"include\": [\"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\"]` which will pick up every TypeScript and TSX file in the repository. After migration, this glob matches `docs/**/*.ts` and `docs/**/*.tsx` — files that are incompatible with the runtime's compiler options. The docs workspace uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\"`, `\"module\": \"esnext\"`, `\"jsx\": \"preserve\"`, and `\"strict\": false`, while the runtime uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"node\"`, `\"module\": \"ES2022\"`, no JSX, and `\"strict\": true`. Running `bun run tc` (which invokes `tsc --noEmit` with the root tsconfig) will fail on docs files unless they are excluded.\n   316→\n   317→Add `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array in the root `tsconfig.json`:\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43c754e8-4bc1-4bd6-9886-b45962e4c4e6","uuid":"11308b42-c77a-4382-a328-c09342df4c52","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n```\n\nVerify the Next.js build succeeds. The `postbuild` step (Pagefind search indexing) should also run. If the build fails, the most likely cause is module resolution issues due to dependency hoisting. Bun workspaces hoist dependencies to the root `node_modules/`. The docs' dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, etc.) will land in the root `node_modules/`, not `docs/node_modules/`. ESM imports from `docs/next.config.mjs` (e.g., `import nextra from 'nextra'`) should resolve via Node's upward traversal, but if they don't, the fallback is to run `bun install` explicitly from `docs/` to create a local `node_modules/` with symlinks.\n\n### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n\n**Step 2.1: Exclude `docs/` from root `tsconfig.json`**\n\nThe root `tsconfig.json` has `\"include\": [\"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\"]` which will pick up every TypeScript and TSX file in the repository. After migration, this glob matches `docs/**/*.ts` and `docs/**/*.tsx` — files that are incompatible with the runtime's compiler options. The docs workspace uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\"`, `\"module\": \"esnext\"`, `\"jsx\": \"preserve\"`, and `\"strict\": false`, while the runtime uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"node\"`, `\"module\": \"ES2022\"`, no JSX, and `\"strict\": true`. Running `bun run tc` (which invokes `tsc --noEmit` with the root tsconfig) will fail on docs files unless they are excluded.\n\nAdd `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array in the root `tsconfig.json`:","numLines":15,"startLine":303,"totalLines":946}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:02:52.494Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZ6QpDUDdNygdZuVAMuBep","type":"tool_result","content":"   633→\n   634→**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n   635→```bash\n   636→bun run generate-schemas\n   637→```\n   638→Verify output exists in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n   639→\n   640→Note: the unified lockfile may resolve slightly different dependency versions than the previous root-only lockfile (e.g., `typescript` may resolve to a newer patch version). This can cause minor cosmetic changes to schema output (a few lines differing in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`). In implementation testing, 4 lines changed in the schema file after the migration's `bun install` step. This is a one-time artifact of the dependency resolution change and is expected — include the schema diff in the migration commit. Future `generate-schemas` runs will be stable.\n   641→\n   642→**Step 6.3: Run the runtime build**\n   643→```bash\n   644→bun run build\n   645→```\n   646→Verify `dist/index.js` is created. The build script uses `import.meta.dir` relative paths and `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point -- these are all unaffected by the workspace addition.\n   647→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43c754e8-4bc1-4bd6-9886-b45962e4c4e6","uuid":"6fbd35d9-202d-4af5-b41b-fcc01945a25d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"\n**Step 6.2: Run schema generation**\n```bash\nbun run generate-schemas\n```\nVerify output exists in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\nNote: the unified lockfile may resolve slightly different dependency versions than the previous root-only lockfile (e.g., `typescript` may resolve to a newer patch version). This can cause minor cosmetic changes to schema output (a few lines differing in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`). In implementation testing, 4 lines changed in the schema file after the migration's `bun install` step. This is a one-time artifact of the dependency resolution change and is expected — include the schema diff in the migration commit. Future `generate-schemas` runs will be stable.\n\n**Step 6.3: Run the runtime build**\n```bash\nbun run build\n```\nVerify `dist/index.js` is created. The build script uses `import.meta.dir` relative paths and `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point -- these are all unaffected by the workspace addition.\n","numLines":15,"startLine":633,"totalLines":946}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:02:52.508Z"}
