{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MngnEP7TzHHa4udrxz1vkt","type":"tool_result","content":"   385→**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `transformPackageJson()`**\n   386→\n   387→At line 173-196 in the `transformPackageJson()` function, add a line to delete the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`:\n   388→\n   389→```typescript\n   390→async function transformPackageJson(packagePath: string): Promise<void> {\n   391→  const content = await readFile(packagePath, \"utf-8\");\n   392→  const pkg = JSON.parse(content);\n   393→\n   394→  pkg.name = \"hankweave\";\n   395→  pkg.publishConfig = { access: \"public\" };\n   396→  pkg.homepage = \"https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime\";\n   397→\n   398→  // Remove monorepo-only fields that don't apply to the public repo\n   399→  delete pkg.workspaces;\n   400→\n   401→  // Remove scripts that reference stripped internal files\n   402→  if (pkg.scripts) {\n   403→    for (const script of STRIP_SCRIPTS) {\n   404→      delete pkg.scripts[script];\n   405→    }\n   406→  }\n   407→\n   408→  await writeFile(packagePath, JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n   409→  // ... logging\n   410→}\n   411→```\n   412→\n   413→The code snippet above shows the full function for context, but the actual edit is minimal: insert `delete pkg.workspaces;` (with a comment) on a new line between line 179 (`pkg.homepage = ...`) and line 181 (`// Remove scripts...`). There is a blank line 180 between these — the insert goes there. Do not rewrite the entire function — the existing `console.log` lines at 189–195 are unchanged.\n   414→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43c754e8-4bc1-4bd6-9886-b45962e4c4e6","uuid":"55877426-70f5-44de-ab3f-bbab60fdfd27","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"**Step 3.2: Update `scripts/sync-public.ts` `transformPackageJson()`**\n\nAt line 173-196 in the `transformPackageJson()` function, add a line to delete the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`:\n\n```typescript\nasync function transformPackageJson(packagePath: string): Promise<void> {\n  const content = await readFile(packagePath, \"utf-8\");\n  const pkg = JSON.parse(content);\n\n  pkg.name = \"hankweave\";\n  pkg.publishConfig = { access: \"public\" };\n  pkg.homepage = \"https://github.com/SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime\";\n\n  // Remove monorepo-only fields that don't apply to the public repo\n  delete pkg.workspaces;\n\n  // Remove scripts that reference stripped internal files\n  if (pkg.scripts) {\n    for (const script of STRIP_SCRIPTS) {\n      delete pkg.scripts[script];\n    }\n  }\n\n  await writeFile(packagePath, JSON.stringify(pkg, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n  // ... logging\n}\n```\n\nThe code snippet above shows the full function for context, but the actual edit is minimal: insert `delete pkg.workspaces;` (with a comment) on a new line between line 179 (`pkg.homepage = ...`) and line 181 (`// Remove scripts...`). There is a blank line 180 between these — the insert goes there. Do not rewrite the entire function — the existing `console.log` lines at 189–195 are unchanged.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":385,"totalLines":946}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:02:56.958Z"}
