{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0114zgVz6jkbQZgo4ADBB8NU","type":"tool_result","content":"   303→**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n   304→\n   305→```bash\n   306→cd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n   307→```\n   308→\n   309→Verify the Next.js build succeeds. The `postbuild` step (Pagefind search indexing) should also run. If the build fails, the most likely cause is module resolution issues due to dependency hoisting. Bun workspaces hoist dependencies to the root `node_modules/`. The docs' dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, etc.) will land in the root `node_modules/`, not `docs/node_modules/`. ESM imports from `docs/next.config.mjs` (e.g., `import nextra from 'nextra'`) should resolve via Node's upward traversal, but if they don't, the fallback is to run `bun install` explicitly from `docs/` to create a local `node_modules/` with symlinks.\n   310→\n   311→**Local dev warning (cosmetic, safe to ignore):** In local development environments where a `package-lock.json` or other lockfile exists higher up the directory tree (e.g., in the user's home directory), Next.js may emit a warning like: \"Next.js inferred your workspace root, but it may not be correct. We detected multiple lockfiles and selected the directory of /Users/.../package-lock.json as the root directory.\" This warning is cosmetic — the build still succeeds. It occurs because Next.js's workspace root detection heuristic scans upward for lockfiles and may find one outside the monorepo. It will not appear in CI or Vercel deployments where the repo is checked out in a clean directory. To silence it locally, add `outputFileTracingRoot: path.resolve(__dirname, '..')` to `docs/next.config.mjs`, but this is optional and not recommended as part of this migration — it adds a config change to the docs site that isn't related to the monorepo structure.\n   312→\n   313→### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n   314→\n   315→**Step 2.1: Exclude `docs/` from root `tsconfig.json`**\n   316→\n   317→The root `tsconfig.json` has `\"include\": [\"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\"]` which will pick up every TypeScript and TSX file in the repository. After migration, this glob matches `docs/**/*.ts` and `docs/**/*.tsx` — files that are incompatible with the runtime's compiler options. The docs workspace uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\"`, `\"module\": \"esnext\"`, `\"jsx\": \"preserve\"`, and `\"strict\": false`, while the runtime uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"node\"`, `\"module\": \"ES2022\"`, no JSX, and `\"strict\": true`. Running `bun run tc` (which invokes `tsc --noEmit` with the root tsconfig) will fail on docs files unless they are excluded.\n   318→\n   319→Add `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array in the root `tsconfig.json`:\n   320→\n   321→```json\n   322→\"exclude\": [\n   323→  \"node_modules\",\n   324→  \".logs/**/*\",\n   325→  \"intermediates/**/*\",\n   326→  \"learning/**/*\",\n   327→  \"tests/test-area/**/*\",\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43c754e8-4bc1-4bd6-9886-b45962e4c4e6","uuid":"5a0db9d4-05e1-4c51-a28a-dfc9aca77e3a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"**Step 1.5: Verify docs build locally**\n\n```bash\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n```\n\nVerify the Next.js build succeeds. The `postbuild` step (Pagefind search indexing) should also run. If the build fails, the most likely cause is module resolution issues due to dependency hoisting. Bun workspaces hoist dependencies to the root `node_modules/`. The docs' dependencies (`next`, `nextra`, `react`, etc.) will land in the root `node_modules/`, not `docs/node_modules/`. ESM imports from `docs/next.config.mjs` (e.g., `import nextra from 'nextra'`) should resolve via Node's upward traversal, but if they don't, the fallback is to run `bun install` explicitly from `docs/` to create a local `node_modules/` with symlinks.\n\n**Local dev warning (cosmetic, safe to ignore):** In local development environments where a `package-lock.json` or other lockfile exists higher up the directory tree (e.g., in the user's home directory), Next.js may emit a warning like: \"Next.js inferred your workspace root, but it may not be correct. We detected multiple lockfiles and selected the directory of /Users/.../package-lock.json as the root directory.\" This warning is cosmetic — the build still succeeds. It occurs because Next.js's workspace root detection heuristic scans upward for lockfiles and may find one outside the monorepo. It will not appear in CI or Vercel deployments where the repo is checked out in a clean directory. To silence it locally, add `outputFileTracingRoot: path.resolve(__dirname, '..')` to `docs/next.config.mjs`, but this is optional and not recommended as part of this migration — it adds a config change to the docs site that isn't related to the monorepo structure.\n\n### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n\n**Step 2.1: Exclude `docs/` from root `tsconfig.json`**\n\nThe root `tsconfig.json` has `\"include\": [\"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\"]` which will pick up every TypeScript and TSX file in the repository. After migration, this glob matches `docs/**/*.ts` and `docs/**/*.tsx` — files that are incompatible with the runtime's compiler options. The docs workspace uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\"`, `\"module\": \"esnext\"`, `\"jsx\": \"preserve\"`, and `\"strict\": false`, while the runtime uses `\"moduleResolution\": \"node\"`, `\"module\": \"ES2022\"`, no JSX, and `\"strict\": true`. Running `bun run tc` (which invokes `tsc --noEmit` with the root tsconfig) will fail on docs files unless they are excluded.\n\nAdd `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array in the root `tsconfig.json`:\n\n```json\n\"exclude\": [\n  \"node_modules\",\n  \".logs/**/*\",\n  \"intermediates/**/*\",\n  \"learning/**/*\",\n  \"tests/test-area/**/*\",","numLines":25,"startLine":303,"totalLines":957}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:06:15.159Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DZfLwY5Jb5yjzUTdVsS9gd","type":"tool_result","content":"   639→```bash\n   640→bun run generate-schemas\n   641→```\n   642→Verify output exists in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n   643→\n   644→Note: schema diffs in the migration commit can come from two sources, both of which are normal and should be included in the commit:\n   645→\n   646→1. **Dependency resolution drift.** The unified lockfile may resolve slightly different dependency versions than the previous root-only lockfile (e.g., `typescript` may resolve to a newer patch version), which can cause minor cosmetic changes to schema output.\n   647→2. **Code changes merged into `develop` since the last schema generation.** If any recently merged PRs added or modified fields in the Zod schemas that feed `generate-schemas`, the regenerated schema JSON will reflect those changes. In implementation testing, the 4-line diff observed in `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` was caused by a `showCosts` field added by a feature PR (`philipn/eng-213-hankweave_runtime_show_costs`), not by dependency resolution. The implementing agent should not assume all schema diffs are from dependency changes — inspect the diff to understand what changed.\n   648→\n   649→In either case, the changes are expected. Include the schema diff in the migration commit. Future `generate-schemas` runs will be stable.\n   650→\n   651→**Step 6.3: Run the runtime build**\n   652→```bash\n   653→bun run build\n   654→```\n   655→Verify `dist/index.js` is created. The build script uses `import.meta.dir` relative paths and `\"./server/index.ts\"` as entry point -- these are all unaffected by the workspace addition.\n   656→\n   657→**Step 6.4: Verify docs build**\n   658→```bash\n   659→cd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n   660→```\n   661→Verify Next.js build succeeds and the `postbuild` Pagefind step runs.\n   662→\n   663→**Step 6.5: Verify npm pack excludes doc